//
// Expected: a0 at one session, a1 at two.
//
// cap_malleable_enc.vp without the `malleable` annotation. ENC is
// unauthenticated, but without the assumption the attacker cannot maul
// ENC(k, CONCAT(lo, lo)) into a ciphertext of its own under k. Bob reaches c
// only through the checked SPLIT, so every substitution fails that check and
// halts him before c is used at all: a0, where the annotated model is a1.
// The pair keeps `malleable` from being either a no-op or a blanket
// authenticity break.
//
// At two sessions c fails without any mauling: it is built from knows
// constants and is the same in every session, so the attacker leaves Alice
// unstarted and replays Alice#2's c to Bob, and Bob and Bob#2 both accept a
// ciphertext Alice sent once. The pair is read at one session.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private k
	knows public lo
	c = ENC(k, CONCAT(lo, lo))
]

Alice -> Bob: c

principal Bob[
	knows private k
	x, y = SPLIT(DEC(k, c))?
	receipt = MAC(k, x)
]

queries[
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: c
]
